index 0000000..688c862
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/restoration/REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Auto Apply and psychotest restoration — review and rollout boundary
+
+This branch changes source code only. It does not change cron, credentials, existing production data, the Render deployment, or the operator live-send switch.
+
+## Auto Apply API
+
+All routes resolve the authenticated Android account to its existing Telegram candidate. A missing or invalid mapping returns HTTP 409 with `code: CANDIDATE_NOT_FOUND`; no candidate is created as a fallback.
+
+- `GET /auto-apply/status`: existing consent/Gmail/CV/operator state plus `diagnosis`, actionable `blockers`, and delivery `summary`. An unavailable Gmail status does not hide the account's saved consent or reporting data.
+- `GET /karirmate/candidates`: real matching contacts plus a structured diagnosis. Empty profile, unreadable/missing CV, no matching opportunities, no eligible contacts, and previously claimed contacts are distinct. Verified active opportunities are ordered before explicitly spontaneous applications.
+- `POST /auto-apply/simulate` with `{}`: read-only plan, maximum remaining daily quota, `mode: simulation`, `sent: 0`, `sending_enabled: false`. It makes no worker calls, queue inserts, claims, history entries, or consent changes. It is a planning simulation; live Gmail, subscription, schedule, worker capability and operator checks still apply when sending.
+- `GET /karirmate/report?period=today|7d|30d|all&offset=0`: account-scoped DB history, 100-row pages and `next_offset`, WIB date filters, confirmed sent totals, failed/pending/uncertain counts, effective remaining quota. Existing undated records remain accessible under `all`.
+
+A delivery is confirmed only with a nonempty Gmail message ID. Ambiguous transport errors stay `uncertain`, consume quota, and are never retried automatically. Do not label these errors as confirmed failures or successes. Legacy `sent` records without an ID are shown as uncertain; legacy undated uncertain records reserve quota conservatively. Pending recipients are deduplicated transactionally before insertion. Existing duplicate ready rows are cancelled when the sender encounters a claim; rows are retained.
+
+The original settings/consent timestamp is retained. No activation or simulation endpoint enables the operator switch or edits scheduling.
+
+## Psychotest access
+
+Short training keeps 10–20 real questions. A full session omits `question_count` and requires verified PRO; it uses the existing configured full length. FREE retains stored score/summary. PRO analysis/question explanations are filtered at both submit and result API boundaries, without altering stored results. All existing bank definitions remain unchanged.
+
+## Local verification
+
+`python -m pip install -r termux/requirements.txt` in a separate virtual environment, then:
+
+```sh
+python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+Tests use temporary SQLite/PDF fixtures and forbid outbound sender HTTP. API integration tests use loopback HTTP. Membership/identity and psychotest API access tests use explicit test fixtures; these do not supply the missing production modules.
+
+## Required before any production rollout
+
+The ten user-named Termux source files are present, but the repository is not a complete deployable snapshot. Still required: the existing `android_auth.py`, `account_access_policy.py`, `karirmate_integrasi_final.py`, `search_identity.py`, `psychotest_bank.py`, and `psychotest_skb.py`. The job/Telegram application also imports `application_methods`, `company_catalog`, `company_search`, `job_catalog`, `job_validation`, `live_sources`, `search_engine`, `idjobs_feed`, `github_search_engine`, `kalibrr_client`, `local_jobs`, `phase4_watch`, and `storage`. A sanitized configuration interface is needed for the missing `config` module; do not commit token values.
+
+The external Gmail worker source is absent. Its refresh behavior, Gmail scope, confirmed `message_id`, idempotency, and explicit spontaneous-application support must be reviewed against the real worker. Do not enable production to test these assumptions.
+
+Contacts need position, location and a traceable source in the existing user-owned tables. Active vacancies additionally need active/verified flags, evidence URL and expiry. Missing fields are reported, not fabricated. Do not alter production tables/data as part of this branch review.
+
+There is no evidence from the user's production database or installed APK in this test environment. The exact production data condition behind the old generic candidate message must be read from the new diagnostic response after an approved rollout. Source-level cause: previous API collapsed reasons to an empty list, and Android discarded the note.
